        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Remove GPT-6 Luna from free model retirement schedule",
        "summary": "The `openai/gpt-6-luna` entry was removed from `FREEBUFF_SCHEDULED_RETIREMENTS` in `common/src/constants/freebuff-model-retirement-schedule.ts`, stopping the two-step retirement mechanism (closesAt, endsAt) for that model. The module now schedules only `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` for retirement. This change reflects the fact that a Respan prompt-cache fix on November 5, 2026 made GPT-6 Luna cheaper to serve than DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, so it remained in the free model picker. Updated comments in `common/src/constants/free-agents.ts` clarify that the project-understanding agent uses GPT-6 Luna on Respan, documenting the routing shift away from the DeepSeek substitution that had been in place since October 30.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In common/src/constants/freebuff-model-retirement-schedule.ts, the `openai/gpt-6-luna` key is removed from `FREEBUFF_SCHEDULED_RETIREMENTS`, leaving only `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`. In common/src/constants/free-agents.ts, the JSDoc for `FREEBUFF_PROJECT_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL_ID` is updated to note that Respan's fix made GPT-6 Luna cheaper to serve than DeepSeek V4.1 Flash.",
