        "title": "CLI model picker applies solo-session discount and shows Free label",
        "summary": "The shared `common` package adds `freebucksRowPrice`, which subtracts the `soloDiscount` from a row's quoted price to determine what admission actually charges, returning the reduced price and the list price to strike beside it. The CLI model selector now calls this helper instead of reading the raw quote, so a solo-session discount lowers the displayed multiplier label or shows \"Free\" when it covers the full cost, and the accent-colour highlight keys off the new `listPrice` return rather than a separate catalog lookup. This aligns the CLI's per-row price display with Desktop and Web, which already draw the solo-discounted price. Tests confirm a 15x row with a 15-point solo discount renders \"Free\" and a 30x row with the same discount renders \"3x\" without the old \"6x\" strike.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/util/freebuff-price-order.ts`, a new export `freebucksRowPrice` is added that computes the charged price as `quoted - soloDiscount` (clamped to 0) and returns a `listPrice` for display. In `cli/src/components/freebuff-model-selector.tsx`, the import shifts from `freebucksListPriceFor` to `freebucksRowPrice`, and the `rowDetails` callback uses the new returned `listPrice` to highlight discounted rows and label a fully discounted row as \"Free\".",
